# ── Secrets and runtime state: never part of a build ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THE ONE THAT MATTERS: .env.shared holds DATABASE_URL (with the password) and ETH_PRIVATE_KEY, and the
# existing `.env` / `.env.local` rules did NOT match it. It was therefore sent to the daemon as build
# context and written into the builder stage on every build. The shipped image is clean — the production
# stage copies only named artifacts — but a credential has no business in a build context or a layer
# cache, and "it does not reach the final image" is a property of the current Dockerfile, not a guarantee.
#
# The rest below are tidiness, and the honest measurement says so. Measured 2026-09-18 on the fleet host:
# the context is 742 MB, of which bls_zk_keys_bls12381_v2 is 344 MB and bls_zk_keys is 243 MB — both
# REQUIRED, both COPYed out of the builder into the final image. data/ is 1.7 MB and had zero files
# modified in a two-minute window, because live validator state lives in Docker volumes
# (validator1_data:/app/data), not in this directory. Excluding it neither shrinks the context
# meaningfully nor stabilises the cache; it is simply correct that runtime state is not a build input.
#
# NOT excluded, deliberately: bls_zk_keys/ and bls_zk_keys_bls12381*/ are COPYed out of the builder into
# the final image (Dockerfile ~line 130). Excluding them produces an image that cannot prove anything.
data/
bft-keys/
.env.shared
.env.shared.*
*.bak
*.bak[0-9]
*.bak-*
*.bak.*
